@startuml View Class Schedule by User
actor User
participant ": ClassDetailPage " as ClassDetailPage
participant ": Router " as Router
participant ": ClassGroupController " as ClassGroupController
participant ": ClassGroupService " as ClassGroupService
participant ": ClassGroupRepository " as ClassGroupRepository
database Database

User->ClassDetailPage: 1. Navigate to Class Detail Page
    activate User
    activate ClassDetailPage

ClassDetailPage->ClassDetailPage: 2. Render Class Detail Page

ClassDetailPage->Router: 3. Send GET /api/classgroup/current-class
    deactivate ClassDetailPage
    activate Router

Router->ClassGroupController: 4. Route Request to Controller
    deactivate Router
    activate ClassGroupController

ClassGroupController->ClassGroupService: 5. GetCurrentClassByUserIdAsync(userId)
    deactivate ClassGroupController
    activate ClassGroupService

ClassGroupService->ClassGroupRepository: 6. GetCurrentClassByUserIdAsync(userId)
    activate ClassGroupRepository

ClassGroupRepository->Database: 7. Query ClassGroup with Schedules by UserId
    activate Database

Database-->ClassGroupRepository: 8. Return ClassGroup with Schedules
    deactivate Database

ClassGroupRepository-->ClassGroupService: 9. Return ClassGroup entity
    deactivate ClassGroupRepository

ClassGroupService->ClassGroupService: 10. Map to ClassGroupDto with Schedules

ClassGroupService-->ClassGroupController: 11. Return ClassGroupDto
    deactivate ClassGroupService
    activate ClassGroupController

ClassGroupController-->Router: 12. Send Class Data Response
    activate Router
    deactivate ClassGroupController

Router-->ClassDetailPage: 13. Display Class Data with Schedules
    activate ClassDetailPage
    deactivate Router

ClassDetailPage->ClassDetailPage: 14. Process and Render Schedule

ClassDetailPage-->User: 15. Show Class Schedule
    deactivate ClassDetailPage
    deactivate User
@enduml

